short:{title:'Short-answer set',paper:'Paper 1 style · SL + HL',intro:'<p>Quick questions of the kind that appear in the short-answer section. Each question is independent.</p>',
 parts:[
 {l:'1',cmd:'State',marks:1,ref:'2.1.1',q:'State one example of an end-of-life user of a bicycle.',award:'Award [1].',pts:['A <b>recycler</b> or scrap dealer who dismantles the bicycle [1]'],acc:'Accept: charity that refurbishes bicycles.',kw:['recycler','end-of-life'],tip:'End-of-life users deal with the product when its use ends.'},
 {l:'2',cmd:'Identify',marks:1,ref:'2.1.4',q:'A designer reads an online forum about how people use standing desks. Identify the type of research.',award:'Award [1].',pts:['<b>Secondary</b> research [1]'],acc:'Do not accept: primary.',kw:['secondary'],tip:'Existing information collected by someone else is secondary.'},
 {l:'3',cmd:'Outline',marks:2,ref:'2.1.2',q:'Outline two disadvantages of user-centred design.',award:'Award [1] for each up to [2 max].',pts:['It is <b>time-consuming and costly</b> because of repeated research and testing [1]','Users may <b>not know or say what they need</b>, or limit the design to small improvements [1]','Constant feedback can cause <b>scope creep</b> [1]'],acc:'Any two.',kw:['time-consuming','costly','scope creep','bias'],tip:'Two brief points, each with a reason.'},
 {l:'4',cmd:'Describe',marks:2,ref:'2.1.4',q:'Describe one situation in which a focus group is a better choice than a survey.',award:'Award [1] for the situation and [1] for the reason.',pts:['When the designer wants to <b>explore opinions or reactions to a prototype</b> [1]','Because the discussion shows <b>why</b> users feel as they do and one person’s idea triggers others [1]'],acc:'Accept other valid situations.',kw:['prototype','why','discussion'],tip:'Give a situation and a reason.'},
 {l:'5',cmd:'Explain',marks:3,ref:'2.1.4',q:'A designer is working on a doorway. Explain why the method of extremes uses the widest and the tallest users.',award:'Award [1] for each valid point up to [3 max].',pts:['Height and width are <b>separate dimensions</b> [1]','The <b>tallest users are not always the widest</b> [1]','Designing for the extremes of each dimension means <b>most users</b> pass through easily [1]'],acc:'Accept use of percentile values.',kw:['extremes','tallest','widest','dimension'],tip:'Each dimension needs its own extreme.'},
 {l:'6',cmd:'Outline',marks:2,ref:'2.1.4',q:'Outline the difference between quantitative and qualitative data, with an example of each.',award:'Award [1] for each of quantitative and qualitative with an example.',pts:['<b>Quantitative</b> is numerical and measurable, for example a rating of 4 out of 5 [1]','<b>Qualitative</b> is descriptive and subjective, for example a comment that the handle “feels cheap” [1]'],acc:'Both sides are needed.',kw:['numerical','descriptive','measurable','subjective'],tip:'Use “whereas” to compare.'},
 {l:'7',cmd:'Explain',marks:2,ref:'2.1.5',q:'Explain why a designer includes a worst-case scenario for a persona.',award:'Award [1] for each valid point up to [2 max].',pts:['It shows <b>the conditions where the product is most likely to fail</b> (tired, rushed, poor light) [1]','So the design can be made <b>safe and usable</b> even in difficult situations [1]'],acc:'Accept a context-specific example.',kw:['worst case','fail','safe','usable'],tip:'Say what the scenario reveals and what the designer does with it.'},
 {l:'8',cmd:'Justify',marks:3,ref:'2.1.5',q:'A game console sold in several countries uses a thumbs-up gesture in its menu. Justify a decision to test this gesture with users in each country.',award:'Award [1] for each valid reason up to [3 max].',pts:['Gestures and symbols are <b>population stereotypes</b> that differ between cultures [1]','A gesture may be <b>offensive or confusing</b> in some places, causing lost sales or harm to the brand [1]','Testing with <b>local users</b> finds the problem before launch, which is cheaper than a recall [1]'],acc:'Accept other valid reasons with evidence.',kw:['stereotype','culture','offensive','testing','local users'],tip:'Give reasons with evidence, not opinions.'}
 ]},

